ggml-webgpu: opt-in perf diagnostics and tuning tokens for the debug harness.

The debug profile string may carry "+"-separated tokens after the profile
name (e.g. "adreno-matvec+sub32+perf"); the profile itself is the first
token. All tokens are off unless the debug harness sets them:

  sub8|sub16|sub32|sub64   kernels per queue submit
  mvwg64|mvwg128|mvwg256   mat-vec (non-MMVQ) workgroup size
  mvo1|mvo2|mvo4|mvo8      mat-vec outputs per workgroup
  perf                     one SAKUTTO_GPUSTAT line per graph: nodes, kernels,
                           submits, CPU encode time, time since the previous
                           graph and time spent waiting in buffer maps
  perfops                  also submit + wait after every op and log per-op
                           wall times (SAKUTTO_GPUOPS), plus the round trip of
                           an empty submit as sync_ms

